  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe following WPT [Image without src/srcset](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/decode/image-decode.html#L93) test image-decode.html is passing for all browsers \nhttps://wpt.fyi/results/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/decode/image-decode.html?label=master&label=experimental&aligned\n\nBut in [dom-img-decode](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#dom-img-decode) nothing says about it.\nAlmos all browsers are checking against nullable [current request](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#current-request) that is non spec conformant.\n\nMay be need to add the following sentence to  [dom-img-decode](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#dom-img-decode) (step 2) \n\n`this's current request's state is unavailable and current URL is empty string then reject promise with an \"EncodingError\" DOMException`\n \n",
